TEACHER EVALUATION SYSTEM (STUDENT FEEDBACK)

Introduction
In today’s educational environment, feedback plays a crucial role in improving the quality of teaching and learning. Traditional methods of evaluating teachers are often paper-based, time-consuming, and may not accurately reflect students’ opinions. Because of these limitations, there is a need for a more efficient and reliable system.

The Teacher Evaluation System (Student Feedback) is designed to collect and manage students’ feedback through a digital platform. This system aims to provide a more organized, accessible, and efficient way of evaluating teachers, helping improve teaching performance and overall educational quality.

Background of the Study
In many schools, teacher evaluations are conducted using printed forms distributed to students. This process can be slow, prone to errors, and difficult to organize. Additionally, students may feel hesitant to give honest feedback due to lack of anonymity.

With the advancement of technology, digital systems offer a better solution for collecting and analyzing feedback. This study focuses on developing a Teacher Evaluation System that allows students to submit their feedback easily and securely while providing accurate results for administrators.

Problem Statement
This study aims to answer the following questions:

How can the process of evaluating teachers be improved?
How can students provide honest and anonymous feedback?
How can evaluation results be collected and analyzed efficiently?
How can the system ensure data accuracy and security?
What features are needed to make the evaluation system effective?

Objectives of the Study

General Objective:
To develop a Teacher Evaluation System that collects student feedback efficiently.

Specific Objectives:

To provide an easy-to-use platform for students
To ensure anonymity of student responses
To automate the collection and analysis of feedback
To generate accurate evaluation reports
To improve the overall teaching performance

Significance of the Study

Students – can express their opinions and experiences openly
Teachers – receive constructive feedback to improve teaching methods
Administrators – gain organized and reliable evaluation data
School – enhances the quality of education and decision-making